outcomes:
  desired:
    - The tool surface covers the full AIDE lifecycle — discover (map),
      read (drill in), scaffold (create with naming enforcement), validate
      (health check), init (one-command bootstrap). Each tool covers a
      distinct lifecycle phase with no overlap between them.
    - Every tool description is complete enough to teach the convention it
      invokes on its own. An agent reading only the tool list learns what
      `.aide` files are, the five file types, the never-both-.aide-and-
      intent.aide naming rule, the next-to-orchestrators placement rule,
      and the read-specs-before-code workflow. No "see docs", no
